        {
          "file": "crates/pm-ui/src/tickets_view.rs",
          "start_line": 1,
          "end_line": 1,
          "rev": "working"
        }
      ],
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "author": "reaganiwadha",
          "created": 1788465000,
          "body": "Implemented per the agreed design. Status: the meta-row chip in the detail pane is now a button; click it for a dropdown of the 5 statuses (check on current), which persists + bumps updated. Closed view: a 'Filter (n/5)' dropdown in the list header is a multi-check of the 5 statuses; unchecked ones are hidden. Default hides Done/Won't Fix. Closed rows that are shown render dim + struck through; header count shows 'N of M' when filtered. Scope kept to PM-11 - no sort (PM-29), no priority editing (PM-4). Needs a run to confirm the popovers behave.",
          "anchor": null
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "author": "reaganiwadha",
          "created": 1788466000,
          "body": "Closing. Status is set from the detail-pane chip dropdown (persists + bumps updated); the list header 'Filter (n/5)' dropdown is a multi-check of the 5 statuses, closed hidden by default, shown-closed rows dim + struck through. Dropdown re-click now closes. Reopen if anything's off.",
          "anchor": null
        }
      ],
      "history": []
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "title": "Ticket priority markers",
      "body": "Two halves that got bundled under one title: **showing** priority in the list, and **setting** it at all. The second is the blocker.\n\n## What exists today\n- The model is complete: `Priority` (Low/Normal/High/Urgent, default Normal) at crates/pm-core/src/pm.rs:76, with `label()` :85 and `color()` :94.\n- The **detail pane** already renders it — a `chip(t.priority.label(), rgb(t.priority.color()), border)` in the meta row, tickets_view.rs:619. Read-only.\n- The **list rows** (tickets_view.rs:378-427) show a status dot `●` tinted by `Status::color()`, the display id, the line `\"{status} · {priority}\"`, and the title. So priority is technically present as text but carries no visual weight — an Urgent ticket looks identical to a Low one at a glance, which is the actual complaint.\n- Nothing anywhere can **change** a priority from the GUI. `PmData::set_priority` exists (pm.rs:448) but has no `AppState` wrapper — see PM-85. The MCP `edit_ticket` tool can already set it (pm-mcp/src/ops.rs:164-224), so today the only way to re-prioritise is through an agent or by hand-editing pm.json5.\n\n## In scope\n**1. A row marker.** Give priority real visual weight in the list. The row already renders a status dot at :378-427, so a second marker needs to not collide with it — a left edge bar, or replacing the dot with a priority-tinted shape, are both plausible; pick one and keep the status colour reachable somehow.\n\n**2. An editable picker.** Clone the `status_button` pattern (tickets_view.rs:549-601) exactly: a chip showing `\"{label} ▾\"` that opens `menu_panel` (:123-180) with one row per priority, each calling the new `AppState::set_priority`. `menu_panel` already takes `(label, dot color, checked, action)` rows, so `Priority::color()` drops straight in. Remember the mutual-exclusion convention — every popover toggle clears `filter_menu_open`/`status_menu_open`/`user_menu_open` (:252-254, :584-586, status_bar.rs:238-240).\n\nNote `Priority` has no `ALL` const the way `Status` does (pm.rs:59) — add one, the picker needs it.\n\n## Depends on\n**PM-85** (AppState mutators) for the picker half. The row marker half has no dependency and can land first.\n\n## Related\n- PM-29 (sort by priority) — this ticket's own earlier comment asked for \"a sorting system or categorization system\"; that's PM-29 for ordering and PM-38 for categorising. Priority sorting is much more useful once markers make priority visible, so PM-29 is the natural follow-on.\n- PM-18 — `Priority::color()` returns raw hex from the data layer, bypassing the theme, so these markers won't survive a light scheme until that's moved onto `ThemeColors`. Tracked there, not here.\n\n## Open question\nShould the list show a marker for **every** priority, or only for above-Normal? Marking all four means most rows carry a Normal-coloured marker that says nothing (Normal is `0xd4d4d4`, the same grey as body text) — showing markers only for High/Urgent, and maybe a dimmed one for Low, would make the signal actually scan.\n\n## Verify\nSet a priority from the GUI, confirm it persists to .pm/pm.json5 and shows up in the ticket's History section (tickets_view.rs:687-707) as a `PriorityChanged` entry with the right author.",
      "status": "open",
      "priority": "high",
      "labels": [
        "tickets"
      ],
      "assignee": null,
      "author": "",
      "created": 1788448518,
      "updated": 1788622460,
      "anchors": [],
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "author": "reaganiwadha",
          "created": 1788448537,
          "body": "This needs to be more detailed, and we need a sorting system or categorization system in tickets",
          "anchor": null
        }
      ],
      "history": [
        {
          "at": 1788622460,
          "author": "claude",
          "kind": "body_changed",
          "old": "",
          "new": "Two halves that got bundled under one title: **showing** priority in the list, and **setting** it at all. The second is the blocker.\n\n## What exists today\n- The model is complete: `Priority` (Low/Normal/High/Urgent, default Normal) at crates/pm-core/src/pm.rs:76, with `label()` :85 and `color()` :94.\n- The **detail pane** already renders it — a `chip(t.priority.label(), rgb(t.priority.color()), border)` in the meta row, tickets_view.rs:619. Read-only.\n- The **list rows** (tickets_view.rs:378-427) show a status dot `●` tinted by `Status::color()`, the display id, the line `\"{status} · {priority}\"`, and the title. So priority is technically present as text but carries no visual weight — an Urgent ticket looks identical to a Low one at a glance, which is the actual complaint.\n- Nothing anywhere can **change** a priority from the GUI. `PmData::set_priority` exists (pm.rs:448) but has no `AppState` wrapper — see PM-85. The MCP `edit_ticket` tool can already set it (pm-mcp/src/ops.rs:164-224), so today the only way to re-prioritise is through an agent or by hand-editing pm.json5.\n\n## In scope\n**1. A row marker.** Give priority real visual weight in the list. The row already renders a status dot at :378-427, so a second marker needs to not collide with it — a left edge bar, or replacing the dot with a priority-tinted shape, are both plausible; pick one and keep the status colour reachable somehow.\n\n**2. An editable picker.** Clone the `status_button` pattern (tickets_view.rs:549-601) exactly: a chip showing `\"{label} ▾\"` that opens `menu_panel` (:123-180) with one row per priority, each calling the new `AppState::set_priority`. `menu_panel` already takes `(label, dot color, checked, action)` rows, so `Priority::color()` drops straight in. Remember the mutual-exclusion convention — every popover toggle clears `filter_menu_open`/`status_menu_open`/`user_menu_open` (:252-254, :584-586, status_bar.rs:238-240).\n\nNote `Priority` has no `ALL` const the way `Status` does (pm.rs:59) — add one, the picker needs it.\n\n## Depends on\n**PM-85** (AppState mutators) for the picker half. The row marker half has no dependency and can land first.\n\n## Related\n- PM-29 (sort by priority) — this ticket's own earlier comment asked for \"a sorting system or categorization system\"; that's PM-29 for ordering and PM-38 for categorising. Priority sorting is much more useful once markers make priority visible, so PM-29 is the natural follow-on.\n- PM-18 — `Priority::color()` returns raw hex from the data layer, bypassing the theme, so these markers won't survive a light scheme until that's moved onto `ThemeColors`. Tracked there, not here.\n\n## Open question\nShould the list show a marker for **every** priority, or only for above-Normal? Marking all four means most rows carry a Normal-coloured marker that says nothing (Normal is `0xd4d4d4`, the same grey as body text) — showing markers only for High/Urgent, and maybe a dimmed one for Low, would make the signal actually scan.\n\n## Verify\nSet a priority from the GUI, confirm it persists to .pm/pm.json5 and shows up in the ticket's History section (tickets_view.rs:687-707) as a `PriorityChanged` entry with the right author."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "title": "The textbox when making a ticket doesn't feel nice",
      "body": "Also I can't ctrl+a copy paste or what",
      "status": "done",
      "priority": "high",
      "labels": [
        "tickets"
      ],
      "assignee": null,
      "author": "",
      "created": 1788448806,
      "updated": 1788466000,
      "anchors": [
        {
          "file": "crates/pm-ui/src/text_input.rs",
          "start_line": 1,
          "end_line": 1,
          "rev": "working"
        }
      ],
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "author": "reaganiwadha",
          "created": 1788449600,
          "body": "Rewrote text_input: selection model + shift-motions, Ctrl+A, cut/copy/paste, Ctrl+Backspace word delete, Up/Down in multiline, and a 1px caret quad that no longer shifts the text. Click focuses the field. Still missing: click-to-place-caret mid-text (needs glyph geometry) — tracked as follow-up.",
          "anchor": null
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "author": "reaganiwadha",
          "created": 1788450076,
          "body": "Still feels awkward. Especially when selecting/highlighting a character from a word you can see each letters jumping. Perhaps we need to see a solution from how zed implements textboxes.",
          "anchor": null
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "author": "reaganiwadha",
          "created": 1788450439,
          "body": "Can't even jump the caret to other section freely with mouse cursor click",
          "anchor": null
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "author": "reaganiwadha",
          "created": 1788460000,
          "body": "Rebuilt text_input the gpui/Zed way (crates/gpui/examples/input.rs): TextInput is now its own entity with a custom Element that shapes each line once via shape_line and paints it as a single ShapedLine — no more glyph jumping. Text arrives through the OS IME pipeline (window.handle_input + EntityInputHandler), so dead keys/compose/AltGr work. Mouse: click places the caret, drag selects, shift-click extends. Editing is actions bound under a 'TextInput' key context in main.rs (Ctrl+A/C/X/V, Ctrl+arrows, Ctrl+Backspace, Home/End, shift-motions, Up/Down); Enter submits single-line, inserts newline in multiline. Single-line fields scroll horizontally to keep the caret visible. Not done: soft-wrap, undo/redo. Needs a run to verify (blocked by a running pm.exe here).",
          "anchor": null
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "author": "reaganiwadha",
          "created": 1788461000,
          "body": "Fixed the startup crash from c4: clicking an empty field put the caret past the end of the zero-length string (index_for_mouse was reading offsets out of the shaped placeholder text). Empty-field click now returns offset 0, and every IME edit range is clamped into content + snapped to a char boundary. Verified: full link + launch smoke test pass. Please restart pm and hammer the New Ticket / comment boxes — click mid-word, drag-select, Ctrl+A/C/V, paste multi-line — then close this if it feels right.",
          "anchor": null
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "author": "reaganiwadha",
          "created": 1788466000,
          "body": "Closing. text_input is now a shaped-line editor entity (gpui/Zed pattern): shape_text per line, IME pipeline, click-to-place-caret + drag-select + shift-click, full Ctrl+A/C/X/V and word/line motions, and the empty-field crash is fixed. Reopen if the feel is still off.",
          "anchor": null
        }
      ],
      "history": []
    },
    {
