        {
          "id": 1,
          "author": "claude",
          "created": 1788622768,
          "body": "**Needs input before it can be scoped.** This is marked `high` priority with the body `\"Description pending\"` and no comments, and nothing in the code identifies which bug it refers to. I went looking and found several candidates rather than one obvious answer:\n\n- **The diff caret.** Gated on focus — `focused: diff_focus.is_focused(window)` (diff_view.rs:448) feeds `CaretView`, so the caret vanishes when the diff pane loses focus. Click-to-focus is at diff_view.rs:886.\n- **The text-input caret.** Separately gated at text_input.rs:1032 (`if focus.is_focused(window)`), with the focus ring at :745/:760 — that pattern is what PM-82 extracts.\n- **The mouse cursor**, not the caret. PM-43 (\"code editor should show a caret rather than a pointer\") is done — this might be a leftover or a regression of it.\n- **Focus not landing where expected** after switching views or opening a modal. The root holds `root_focus` specifically so keybindings dispatch before the diff pane is focused (app.rs:143-145), and Escape runs a dismiss ladder (app.rs:968-978) — plausible places for focus to end up somewhere surprising.\n- Or the **Wayland drag issue** (PM-21), which is cursor-related but already tracked separately.\n\nSome of these are covered by the PM-81 focus work (PM-82/83/84) and would close for free; others are real bugs that would survive it.\n\n@reaganiwadha — which cursor, and what does it do wrong? Given the `high` priority it's worth pinning down rather than leaving it to be rediscovered.",
          "anchor": null
        }
      ],
      "history": [
        {
          "at": 1788622768,
          "author": "claude",
          "kind": "commented",
          "comment_id": 1
        }
      ]
    },
