      "id": 14,
      "title": "installscript for windows, and github pointed auto update system",
      "body": "",
      "status": "done",
      "priority": "low",
      "labels": [],
      "assignee": null,
      "author": "",
      "created": 1788449089,
      "updated": 1788495402,
      "anchors": [],
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "author": "reaganiwadha",
          "created": 1788449099,
          "body": "This needs further elaboration on how I want it",
          "anchor": null
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "author": "claude",
          "created": 1788484746,
          "body": "First pass landed. pm is now a SINGLE binary with subcommands (src/cli.rs): pm [<path>] = GUI, pm mcp, pm update, pm --version, pm --help. crates/pm-mcp is now a library folded into the pm bin (pm_mcp::serve_stdio). install.ps1 at the repo root (served raw from trunk) does irm|iex -> %LOCALAPPDATA%/Programs/pm + SHA256 verify + user PATH; -Version <tag> pins. Auto-update v1: pm_core::update::latest() checks the GitHub releases API on startup (bg thread); a newer release shows as a status-bar chip and an About line. pm update (Windows) downloads pm.exe.new, renames the running exe to pm.exe.old, swaps, relaunches; cleanup_stale() drops the .old next start. Non-GUI subcommands AttachConsole so output shows under windows_subsystem=windows. Not code-signed -> SmartScreen warning (noted in README). macOS/Linux pm update deferred.",
          "anchor": null
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "author": "claude",
          "created": 1788495362,
          "body": "Done. install.ps1 (irm | iex → %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Programs\\pm, SHA256 verify, user PATH, then runs `pm --setup`) + `pm --update` self-updater (crates/pm-core/src/update.rs: checks GitHub releases/latest, downloads pm.exe, rename-swaps the running exe, relaunches). GitHub-pointed: REPO = GecEnterprises/pm throughout. Status-bar update chip + About-box line when a newer release exists. Releases v0.0.1–v0.0.3 all shipped through this. See also PM-27 (release CI) and PM-5 (pm --setup).",
          "anchor": null
        }
      ],
      "history": []
    },
