      "id": 16,
      "title": "Tab navigation",
      "body": "",
      "status": "open",
      "priority": "normal",
      "labels": [],
      "assignee": null,
      "author": "",
      "created": 1788449479,
      "updated": 1788622759,
      "anchors": [],
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "author": "claude",
          "created": 1788622759,
          "body": "**Probable duplicate — flagging rather than inventing a scope.** The title is one line with no body and could mean at least three different things, so I'd rather ask than guess:\n\n1. **Tab between form inputs** — that's PM-28 (symptom) / PM-84 (implementation), both open and now fully specced.\n2. **Tab between the top-level views** (Summary / File-to-File / Tickets) — already shipped as PM-19, bound to `ctrl-tab`/`ctrl-shift-tab` (src/main.rs:89-90, `cycle_view` at app.rs:504-513).\n3. **Editor-style tabs** — multiple open files as a tab strip across the diff view. Nothing like this exists; it would be a genuinely new feature and overlaps PM-67 (multi-project workspace) and PM-53 (a header bar over the File-to-File view).\n\nIf it's (1) or (2), this can be closed as a duplicate. If it's (3), it wants a real body and probably a different title, since \"tab navigation\" reads as (1) to anyone picking it up cold.\n\n@reaganiwadha — which was it?",
          "anchor": null
        }
      ],
      "history": [
        {
          "at": 1788622759,
          "author": "claude",
          "kind": "commented",
          "comment_id": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
