    {
      "id": 34,
      "title": "pm.json5 alternative storage engine/option.",
      "body": "Users can choose whether to store database of pm work in .pm in the repository, or store it locally in ~/.pm/path-to-project-in-strips/. For this to work, we need a layer of persistance working. Keyval db works no need sqlite i think.",
      "status": "done",
      "priority": "normal",
      "labels": [],
      "assignee": null,
      "author": "",
      "created": 1788475247,
      "updated": 1788584041,
      "anchors": [
        {
          "file": "crates/pm-core/src/config.rs",
          "start_line": 1,
          "end_line": 1,
          "rev": "working"
        }
      ],
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "author": "reaganiwadha",
          "created": 1788467000,
          "body": "Persistence layer done (needed before PM-36). crates/pm-core/src/config.rs is a plain-JSON key/value document - no sqlite - at ~/.pm/config.json, with atomic writes and defaults on missing/broken. crates/pm-ui/src/config.rs exposes it as a gpui global: ConfigStore::get(cx) / ConfigStore::update(cx, |c| ...) (persist + refresh_windows). Loaded in main.rs; writes the default file on first run. First field is ui_scale. Verified: unit tests + hand-edited ui_scale=1.75 survives a restart. Still open on this ticket: letting the user choose where PROJECT ticket data lives (in-repo .pm/pm.json5 vs ~/.pm/<slug>/) - that needs pm_core::pm load/save to take a path.",
          "anchor": null
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "author": "claude",
          "created": 1788584041,
          "body": "Done. ~/.pm/config.json gains a `stores` registry (project root -> in_repo | home + resolved dir); pm_core::Config::resolve_store_dir/set_store/project_slug are the single choke point pm::load_in/save_in, AppState, the watcher, and pm-mcp all route through. The Tickets view (not the diff view — diffing never prompts) shows a modal the first time it's opened for a project with no .pm/ and no saved choice: \"In this repository\" (preselected, Esc accepts it) vs \"In ~/.pm (outside the repo)\", landing at ~/.pm/projects/<slug>/pm.json5. Sentinel::start takes an optional extra watch path so an external store still triggers a live reload. pm-mcp's resolve_root / list_projects consult the same registry so externally-stored projects stay visible to the MCP tools. Follow-ups (separate tickets): moving an existing project's store after the fact, a File-menu control for it, seeding project.name from the folder.",
          "anchor": null
        }
      ],
      "history": []
    },
