    {
      "id": 38,
      "title": "Ticket tagging",
      "body": "Each ticket should carry multiple tags so the list can be organised by them (`ui`, `ux`, `mcp`, …).\n\n## Most of this already exists — it's a UI-only ticket\n`Ticket.labels: Vec<String>` has been in the model all along (crates/pm-core/src/pm.rs:176). Concretely, already working:\n- `PmData::set_labels` (pm.rs:496) with a `LabelsChanged` history event.\n- The MCP `edit_ticket` tool sets them (pm-mcp/src/ops.rs:164-224) and `list_tickets` **already filters by label** (ops.rs:96-107).\n- The detail pane renders each one as a `chip` tinted `colors.changed` (tickets_view.rs:620-622).\n- Real tickets in this very project are already labelled — `fremantle`, `tickets`, `ui`, `mcp`, `bug`.\n\nSo the gap is narrow and specific: **no editor and no filter in the GUI.** Labels can only be set by an agent through MCP or by hand-editing pm.json5, and the ticket list can't be narrowed by one.\n\n## First: settle the terminology\nThe model says **labels**; this ticket says **tags**. Two names for one field will confuse everything downstream (the MCP arg is already `label`). Pick one and use it everywhere — recommend keeping `labels`, since it's the name already on disk in every existing pm.json5 and in the MCP tool signature, and renaming the serialized field would break older readers (see PM-86).\n\n## In scope\n**1. A label editor in the detail pane.** The chips at :620-622 become editable — add/remove, with a text input for new ones. Worth offering completion from labels already used in the project (collect the distinct set across `state.pm.tickets`); free-text-only guarantees `ui` and `UI` and `ux ` diverge immediately.\n\n**2. Label filtering in the list.** The status filter is already there and is the pattern to follow: `ticket_filter: HashSet<Status>` (app.rs:182), `filter_button` (tickets_view.rs:217-269) opening a `menu_panel` checklist (:123-180), applied in `shown_tickets` (:274-286). A label filter is the same shape with a `HashSet<String>` — but note `shown_tickets` now composes **two** filters (status + PM-75's search), and this makes three. They must AND together, not replace each other.\n\n## Depends on\n**PM-85** (AppState mutators) — `set_labels` has no `AppState` wrapper, same as the other four fields.\n\n## Related\n- **PM-63** (make the active filter obvious) — the `filter_button` label is already the unhelpful hardcoded `\"Filter (n/5) ▾\"` (:244-247). Adding a second filter dimension makes that strictly worse, so PM-63 should probably land alongside or before this, not after.\n- **PM-50** (linking/hierarchy) lists \"lean on labels\" as one of its options — if this ticket ships a good label editor, that option gets cheaper.\n\n## Open questions\n- Free-form strings, or a project-level registry of allowed labels in pm.json5 (which would give them stable colours)? Right now every chip is the same `colors.changed` tint, so ten labels are visually indistinguishable.\n- Should the list rows show labels at all, or only the detail pane? Rows are already carrying a status dot, id, status·priority, title — and PM-4 and PM-66 both want to add more.\n\n## Verify\nAdd and remove a label in the GUI, confirm it persists to .pm/pm.json5, appears as a `LabelsChanged` history entry, and that the same label filters correctly through both the GUI list and `mcp__pm__list_tickets(label: ...)`.",
      "status": "open",
      "priority": "normal",
      "labels": [],
      "assignee": null,
      "author": "",
      "created": 1788477949,
      "updated": 1788622497,
      "anchors": [],
      "comments": [],
      "history": [
        {
          "at": 1788622497,
          "author": "claude",
          "kind": "body_changed",
          "old": "Each ticket should be able to be tagged with a certain tag so we can organize a view of tickets with a ui tag or ux tag or mcp tag. each ticket can have multiple tags",
          "new": "Each ticket should carry multiple tags so the list can be organised by them (`ui`, `ux`, `mcp`, …).\n\n## Most of this already exists — it's a UI-only ticket\n`Ticket.labels: Vec<String>` has been in the model all along (crates/pm-core/src/pm.rs:176). Concretely, already working:\n- `PmData::set_labels` (pm.rs:496) with a `LabelsChanged` history event.\n- The MCP `edit_ticket` tool sets them (pm-mcp/src/ops.rs:164-224) and `list_tickets` **already filters by label** (ops.rs:96-107).\n- The detail pane renders each one as a `chip` tinted `colors.changed` (tickets_view.rs:620-622).\n- Real tickets in this very project are already labelled — `fremantle`, `tickets`, `ui`, `mcp`, `bug`.\n\nSo the gap is narrow and specific: **no editor and no filter in the GUI.** Labels can only be set by an agent through MCP or by hand-editing pm.json5, and the ticket list can't be narrowed by one.\n\n## First: settle the terminology\nThe model says **labels**; this ticket says **tags**. Two names for one field will confuse everything downstream (the MCP arg is already `label`). Pick one and use it everywhere — recommend keeping `labels`, since it's the name already on disk in every existing pm.json5 and in the MCP tool signature, and renaming the serialized field would break older readers (see PM-86).\n\n## In scope\n**1. A label editor in the detail pane.** The chips at :620-622 become editable — add/remove, with a text input for new ones. Worth offering completion from labels already used in the project (collect the distinct set across `state.pm.tickets`); free-text-only guarantees `ui` and `UI` and `ux ` diverge immediately.\n\n**2. Label filtering in the list.** The status filter is already there and is the pattern to follow: `ticket_filter: HashSet<Status>` (app.rs:182), `filter_button` (tickets_view.rs:217-269) opening a `menu_panel` checklist (:123-180), applied in `shown_tickets` (:274-286). A label filter is the same shape with a `HashSet<String>` — but note `shown_tickets` now composes **two** filters (status + PM-75's search), and this makes three. They must AND together, not replace each other.\n\n## Depends on\n**PM-85** (AppState mutators) — `set_labels` has no `AppState` wrapper, same as the other four fields.\n\n## Related\n- **PM-63** (make the active filter obvious) — the `filter_button` label is already the unhelpful hardcoded `\"Filter (n/5) ▾\"` (:244-247). Adding a second filter dimension makes that strictly worse, so PM-63 should probably land alongside or before this, not after.\n- **PM-50** (linking/hierarchy) lists \"lean on labels\" as one of its options — if this ticket ships a good label editor, that option gets cheaper.\n\n## Open questions\n- Free-form strings, or a project-level registry of allowed labels in pm.json5 (which would give them stable colours)? Right now every chip is the same `colors.changed` tint, so ten labels are visually indistinguishable.\n- Should the list rows show labels at all, or only the detail pane? Rows are already carrying a status dot, id, status·priority, title — and PM-4 and PM-66 both want to add more.\n\n## Verify\nAdd and remove a label in the GUI, confirm it persists to .pm/pm.json5, appears as a `LabelsChanged` history entry, and that the same label filters correctly through both the GUI list and `mcp__pm__list_tickets(label: ...)`."
        }
      ]
    },
