    {
      "id": 54,
      "title": "Squiggling lines/shaky lines when scrolling in the code viewer. Each line would randomly go up and down sometimes. Investigate why and investigate why zed doesn't have this issue.",
      "body": "",
      "status": "done",
      "priority": "normal",
      "labels": [],
      "assignee": null,
      "author": "reaganiwadha",
      "created": 1788494128,
      "updated": 1788495399,
      "anchors": [],
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "author": "claude",
          "created": 1788495355,
          "body": "Done (commit bd73414).\n\nRoot cause: the custom scrolling elements (diff_view, list_view, tree_view, history_view) computed row_h = CONST * zoom_ratio with no rounding, so at any non-100% zoom the row height is fractional — 18 * 1.1 = 19.8px at 110% (which is where you were). gpui's paint_glyph quantises each glyph baseline to 1/4 of a physical pixel, so with a fractional row height y = base + i*19.8 lands each line on a different quarter-pixel and the gap between consecutive lines wobbles ±1/4px as the scroll offset moves — the shake.\n\nWhy Zed doesn't have it: gpui's own TextStyle::line_height_in_pixels does .round(), so Zed's editor always gets a whole-pixel line height. pm's custom element bypassed that path.\n\nFix: row_h = (CONST * s).round() in the four elements + Pm::diff_row_h (the scroll math must match the paint). An integer logical row height is a clean multiple of 1/4 physical px at every common Windows display scale (100/125/150/175/200%). Sub-pixel-smooth scrolling is preserved (the scroll offset itself is not rounded).",
          "anchor": null
        }
      ],
      "history": []
    },
    {
      "id": 55,
      "title": "Vendor a new package named fremantle which is just gpui components both primitives and scaffolding for it to be used in other applications. That way, pm-ui is a constrcution of the ui based off those primitives",
      "body": "Goal: a new `crates/fremantle` workspace member holding generic, domain-agnostic gpui primitives + scaffolding, so pm-ui becomes a consumer built on top of it rather than defining everything inline.\n\n## Constraint\nfremantle is a **composable primitives library**, not shaped to pm-ui's or any specific app's domain. A second gpui app is planned (zagtag) but it currently has zero gpui code (Electron+React today) — do not design primitives around its domain shape either. Judge the API on its own merits.\n\n## Current state (why this is scoped the way it is)\n- pm-ui already depends on `gpui` directly (git dep on `zed-industries/zed`, branch `main`) — there's no existing internal UI crate to split from; fremantle is entirely new.\n- `scroll.rs` (pure math, zero gpui-domain coupling) and `decorations.rs` (window chrome, only touches theme constants) are already domain-free and can move near-verbatim.\n- `text_input.rs` (971 lines) is a full custom `Element` (IME, single/multiline, actions-based editing) that's domain-free but incomplete — its own doc comment says \"not handled: undo/redo\" — and PM-2 is blocked specifically on this widget not being production-ready.\n- `theme.rs` (81 lines) is flat `pub const` hex colors + metrics, no struct, no light/dark support — this is what PM-18 (\"Color Scheming System\") is asking for. Every one of pm-ui's 15+ view files does `use crate::theme::*`, so migrating this is the highest-touch step.\n- `list_view.rs` / `tree_view.rs` / `history_view.rs` share a generic virtualized-row/scrollbar rendering pattern but are entangled with `Entity<Pm>` (the app's domain entity) — extracting the pattern needs a delegate/trait abstraction.\n- `icons.rs` bundles SVGs via `include_dir!` pointed at pm-ui's own `assets/` dir — needs to accept an asset source from the consumer instead.\n\n## In scope\nNew `crates/fremantle` workspace member (`gpui = { workspace = true }`, same git pin as pm-ui, path-dep from pm-ui like pm-core today); extracting **and generalizing** (not just moving) scroll, decorations, theme, text-input, icons, and the list/row rendering pattern; migrating pm-ui to consume them.\n\nThis folds in PM-2 (text-input blocker) and PM-18 (color system gap) — both get resolved as fremantle's first primitives rather than tracked separately.\n\n## Out of scope\nPorting zagtag to gpui; publishing fremantle externally; `app.rs`/`config.rs`/`update.rs` (stay pm-specific); `menu.rs`/`status_bar.rs`/`title_bar.rs` (defer, not required for v1).\n\n## Phasing (tracked as sub-tickets)\n1. Scaffold `crates/fremantle` + move `scroll.rs`, `decorations.rs` near-verbatim — proves workspace wiring.\n2. Theme system (closes PM-18): `Theme` struct replacing flat consts, instantiable per-consumer; migrate all `use crate::theme::*` call sites.\n3. TextInput primitive (unblocks PM-2): move `text_input.rs`, add undo/redo, confirm/extend API against its usage in `diff_view.rs:698-970`.\n4. Icons: move `icons.rs`, parameterize asset source instead of baking in pm-ui's `assets/` dir.\n5. Generic list/row primitive: delegate-based `fremantle::list` extracted from `list_view.rs`/`tree_view.rs`/`history_view.rs`; rebuild the three call sites as thin delegates. Largest/riskiest, done last.\n\nVerify each phase with `cargo check`/`cargo build` across the workspace plus a visual smoke-test of pm-ui.",
      "status": "open",
      "priority": "normal",
      "labels": [],
      "assignee": null,
      "author": "unknown",
      "created": 1788494930,
      "updated": 1788590645,
      "anchors": [],
      "comments": [],
      "history": []
    },
    {
