        {
          "id": 1,
          "author": "claude",
          "created": 1788584041,
          "body": "Done. Status bar shows an \"Acting as <name>\" chip (git user.name by default via resolve_author) — click it for a popover with a free-text name field, \"Use git username\", and \"Reset to git default\" (clears Config.author). The choice persists to ~/.pm/config.json, syncing across windows. Removed the old inline \"as:\" fields from the new-ticket/comment forms — the status-bar section is now the single place to set the author. Also fixed a related bug: a window opened empty resolved to \"unknown\" and the popover field stayed stale after a folder was picked — load_repo now re-seeds it.",
          "anchor": null
        }
      ],
      "history": []
    },
    {
      "id": 57,
      "title": "Should be able to change a ticket title, and clicking on the ticket title will show an input",
      "body": "## What exists today\nThe ticket title in the detail pane is a plain read-only `div` — `text_size(17.0)`, `t.title`, tickets_view.rs:649-654. There is no click handler and no edit path. `PmData::set_title` (crates/pm-core/src/pm.rs:398) already exists, already records a `TitleChanged` history event, and is already reachable from the MCP `edit_ticket` tool (pm-mcp/src/ops.rs:164-224) — the GUI is the only side that can't rename a ticket.\n\n## In scope\nClick the title → swap the `div` for an inline `TextInput::single` seeded with the current title; Enter or blur commits via the new `AppState::set_title`, Escape cancels.\n\nMechanics that are already solved elsewhere in this file:\n- `TextInput::single(cx).text(...)` + `.focus(window, cx)` — the constructor pattern is at app.rs:210-232, and `focus()` is called imperatively from three places already (tickets_view.rs:83, :206, :356).\n- Enter-to-commit — `new_ticket_title` subscribes to `TextInputEvent::Submit` (app.rs:211-215) and that drives `submit_new_ticket` (tickets_view.rs:794-804). Same wiring.\n- Escape — the root already runs a dismiss ladder in `on_key_down` (app.rs:968-978, store modal → open menu → About). A title edit in progress needs a rung on that ladder, or it'll fall through and dismiss something else.\n\n**Save on commit, not on `Changed`.** `AppState::save_pm` (state.rs:211) rewrites the whole pm.json5 on every call, and `PmData::set_title` pushes a history entry per distinct value — subscribing to `Changed` would write the file and a `TitleChanged` entry on every keystroke.\n\nWhere the new `TextInput` entity lives is the one real design call: the five existing ones are long-lived fields on `Pm` (app.rs:166-175) built once in `Pm::new`. A sixth (`title_edit: Option<Entity<TextInput>>`, or a permanent one plus an `editing_title: bool`) fits that pattern; the permanent-entity version is simpler and matches what's already there.\n\n## Depends on\n**PM-85** (AppState mutators). Nothing else.\n\n## Out of scope — but note the neighbours\nThe **body** has exactly the same gap (rendered read-only through `text_block`, tickets_view.rs:657-659) and the same missing wrapper. Deliberately not folded in here, because PM-8/PM-9 want to change how the body *renders* (markdown), and editing it is much easier to design once that's settled. If body editing is wanted before markdown lands, it's a near-copy of this ticket.\n\nSame story for labels (PM-38) and assignee — all read-only chips in the meta row (:620-629), all unblocked by PM-85.\n\n## Open question\nIs click-anywhere-on-the-title the right affordance, or does it need a hover cue / explicit edit icon? A bare click-to-edit on a 17px heading is easy to trigger by accident when you meant to select text.\n\n## Verify\nRename a ticket, confirm the new title persists to .pm/pm.json5, shows in the list row (:412) and the window title (app.rs:404), and appears in the History section (:687-707) as a `TitleChanged` entry with old and new values.",
      "status": "open",
      "priority": "normal",
      "labels": [],
      "assignee": null,
      "author": "unknown",
      "created": 1788495141,
      "updated": 1788622476,
      "anchors": [],
      "comments": [],
      "history": [
        {
          "at": 1788622476,
          "author": "claude",
          "kind": "body_changed",
          "old": "",
          "new": "## What exists today\nThe ticket title in the detail pane is a plain read-only `div` — `text_size(17.0)`, `t.title`, tickets_view.rs:649-654. There is no click handler and no edit path. `PmData::set_title` (crates/pm-core/src/pm.rs:398) already exists, already records a `TitleChanged` history event, and is already reachable from the MCP `edit_ticket` tool (pm-mcp/src/ops.rs:164-224) — the GUI is the only side that can't rename a ticket.\n\n## In scope\nClick the title → swap the `div` for an inline `TextInput::single` seeded with the current title; Enter or blur commits via the new `AppState::set_title`, Escape cancels.\n\nMechanics that are already solved elsewhere in this file:\n- `TextInput::single(cx).text(...)` + `.focus(window, cx)` — the constructor pattern is at app.rs:210-232, and `focus()` is called imperatively from three places already (tickets_view.rs:83, :206, :356).\n- Enter-to-commit — `new_ticket_title` subscribes to `TextInputEvent::Submit` (app.rs:211-215) and that drives `submit_new_ticket` (tickets_view.rs:794-804). Same wiring.\n- Escape — the root already runs a dismiss ladder in `on_key_down` (app.rs:968-978, store modal → open menu → About). A title edit in progress needs a rung on that ladder, or it'll fall through and dismiss something else.\n\n**Save on commit, not on `Changed`.** `AppState::save_pm` (state.rs:211) rewrites the whole pm.json5 on every call, and `PmData::set_title` pushes a history entry per distinct value — subscribing to `Changed` would write the file and a `TitleChanged` entry on every keystroke.\n\nWhere the new `TextInput` entity lives is the one real design call: the five existing ones are long-lived fields on `Pm` (app.rs:166-175) built once in `Pm::new`. A sixth (`title_edit: Option<Entity<TextInput>>`, or a permanent one plus an `editing_title: bool`) fits that pattern; the permanent-entity version is simpler and matches what's already there.\n\n## Depends on\n**PM-85** (AppState mutators). Nothing else.\n\n## Out of scope — but note the neighbours\nThe **body** has exactly the same gap (rendered read-only through `text_block`, tickets_view.rs:657-659) and the same missing wrapper. Deliberately not folded in here, because PM-8/PM-9 want to change how the body *renders* (markdown), and editing it is much easier to design once that's settled. If body editing is wanted before markdown lands, it's a near-copy of this ticket.\n\nSame story for labels (PM-38) and assignee — all read-only chips in the meta row (:620-629), all unblocked by PM-85.\n\n## Open question\nIs click-anywhere-on-the-title the right affordance, or does it need a hover cue / explicit edit icon? A bare click-to-edit on a 17px heading is easy to trigger by accident when you meant to select text.\n\n## Verify\nRename a ticket, confirm the new title persists to .pm/pm.json5, shows in the list row (:412) and the window title (app.rs:404), and appears in the History section (:687-707) as a `TitleChanged` entry with old and new values."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 58,
      "title": "Historical lineage of what happens to a ticket should be preserved, we need a richer struct/json format for this. Description changes, title changes, when did it gets done, everything",
      "body": "",
      "status": "done",
      "priority": "normal",
      "labels": [],
      "assignee": null,
      "author": "unknown",
      "created": 1788495204,
      "updated": 1788585339,
      "anchors": [],
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "author": "Claude",
          "created": 1788585096,
          "body": "Implemented: Ticket gains a `history: Vec<HistoryEntry>` field (pm-core/src/pm.rs), oldest-first. Each entry is `{ at, author, kind: ... }` via a typed `HistoryEvent` enum: TitleChanged/BodyChanged/StatusChanged/PriorityChanged/LabelsChanged/AssigneeChanged (old/new) and Commented { comment_id } (points at the comment rather than duplicating its text). Every mutating setter (set_title/set_body/set_status/set_priority/set_assignee/set_labels/add_comment) now takes an `author` and pushes an entry when something actually changes.\n\nAuthor threading: `AppState::set_ticket_status` and MCP's `edit_ticket` now resolve/accept `author` the same way create_ticket/add_comment already did (PM-15 convention) — edit_ticket gained an `author` param. GUI status changes pass `None` (falls back to the window's \"Acting as\" identity).\n\nUI: ticket_detail now renders a \"History\" section (tickets_view.rs) above Comments — one line per entry: relative time + a plain-English description (\"carol changed status: open → done\").\n\nOld tickets with no `history` field deserialize fine (`#[serde(default)]`, empty vec) — no migration needed. Added pm-mcp test `history_records_edits_and_comments` covering comment + title + status entries end-to-end. Full workspace test suite passes.",
          "anchor": null
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "author": "Claude",
          "created": 1788585339,
          "body": "Verified live: the running GUI itself exercised this — a comment and two status flips on PM-44 recorded correctly in its history array (commented → status_changed open→blocked → status_changed blocked→open), and every pre-existing ticket backfilled with an empty history: [] on save. Committed and pushed (976ad61); no release cut for this one.",
          "anchor": null
        }
      ],
      "history": []
    },
