    {
      "id": 68,
      "title": "pm readme.md human rewrite",
      "body": "",
      "status": "open",
      "priority": "normal",
      "labels": [],
      "assignee": null,
      "author": "reaganiwadha",
      "created": 1788590440,
      "updated": 1788590462,
      "anchors": [],
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "author": "reaganiwadha",
          "created": 1788590462,
          "body": "Rewrite the readme.md by reaganiwadha, do not vibe write the readme.md",
          "anchor": null
        }
      ],
      "history": []
    },
    {
      "id": 69,
      "title": "Nested comments",
      "body": "## What exists today\n`Comment` (crates/pm-core/src/pm.rs:121-133) is flat: `id`, `author`, `created`, `body`, `anchor`. No parent, no thread id. Comments render as a plain sequence — `\"{author} · {rel_time}\"` plus `text_block(&c.body)` per comment, tickets_view.rs:710-738 — with a single composer underneath (:740-769).\n\n## The schema change is one line. The rest isn't.\nAdding `parent: Option<u64>` with `#[serde(default)]` is trivially backward-compatible. What assumes a flat list:\n\n- **Comment ids are `max(id)+1` scoped per ticket** (pm.rs:531). Fine for a tree, but it means ids are only meaningful within their ticket — a parent reference can't be validated across tickets, and nothing today checks that a parent exists or that the graph is acyclic.\n- **`HistoryEvent::Commented { comment_id }`** (pm.rs:149) and the merged timeline. `history_line` (:47-72) and the History section (:687-707) render one flat chronological list; a reply is still a chronological event, so this probably still works — but check it reads sensibly rather than assuming it.\n- **There is one `comment_box` for the whole ticket** — a single `Entity<TextInput>` field on `Pm` (app.rs:168, `TextInput::multi`). Per-reply composers mean either N text inputs or one that relocates. N inputs interacts directly with **PM-84** (tab/roving focus order), which is already counting the five that exist today.\n- **`add_comment` on the MCP side** (pm-mcp/src/ops.rs:117-134) needs a `parent` arg, or agents can only ever post at top level.\n\n## Rendering\nIndentation in the comment list (:710-738) is the easy part. Decide the depth policy up front — unbounded nesting on a resizable sidebar-width pane degrades fast. Two levels (comment + replies, no deeper) is what most trackers settle on and is much cheaper to render and to focus-manage.\n\n## Depends on / related\n- **PM-86** (`version` written but never read) — this is precisely the field that an older `pm` binary would silently drop on its next save, taking every reply's parent link with it and flattening the thread irreversibly. Strongly prefer landing PM-86's guard first; if that's not wanted, at least know the exposure.\n- **PM-84** — per-reply composers multiply focusable inputs.\n- **PM-2** (line-anchored comments from the diff gutter) — `Comment.anchor` (pm.rs:132) already exists and is unblocked now that PM-72 shipped. A threaded reply to an anchored comment should presumably inherit or ignore the anchor; worth settling once rather than twice.\n\n## Open question\nIs this actually wanted for **comments**, or for **replies to review comments** (the PM-2 diff-gutter flow)? Threading matters much more in a code-review context than on a ticket. If PM-2 is the real motivation, this should probably follow it rather than lead.\n\n## Verify\nPost a reply, confirm it persists to .pm/pm.json5 with the right `parent`, renders indented, survives a round-trip through both the GUI and `mcp__pm__get_ticket`, and that an existing flat ticket (every comment in this project today) still renders unchanged.",
      "status": "open",
      "priority": "normal",
      "labels": [],
      "assignee": null,
      "author": "reaganiwadha",
      "created": 1788590649,
      "updated": 1788622565,
      "anchors": [],
      "comments": [],
      "history": [
        {
          "at": 1788622565,
          "author": "claude",
          "kind": "body_changed",
          "old": "",
          "new": "## What exists today\n`Comment` (crates/pm-core/src/pm.rs:121-133) is flat: `id`, `author`, `created`, `body`, `anchor`. No parent, no thread id. Comments render as a plain sequence — `\"{author} · {rel_time}\"` plus `text_block(&c.body)` per comment, tickets_view.rs:710-738 — with a single composer underneath (:740-769).\n\n## The schema change is one line. The rest isn't.\nAdding `parent: Option<u64>` with `#[serde(default)]` is trivially backward-compatible. What assumes a flat list:\n\n- **Comment ids are `max(id)+1` scoped per ticket** (pm.rs:531). Fine for a tree, but it means ids are only meaningful within their ticket — a parent reference can't be validated across tickets, and nothing today checks that a parent exists or that the graph is acyclic.\n- **`HistoryEvent::Commented { comment_id }`** (pm.rs:149) and the merged timeline. `history_line` (:47-72) and the History section (:687-707) render one flat chronological list; a reply is still a chronological event, so this probably still works — but check it reads sensibly rather than assuming it.\n- **There is one `comment_box` for the whole ticket** — a single `Entity<TextInput>` field on `Pm` (app.rs:168, `TextInput::multi`). Per-reply composers mean either N text inputs or one that relocates. N inputs interacts directly with **PM-84** (tab/roving focus order), which is already counting the five that exist today.\n- **`add_comment` on the MCP side** (pm-mcp/src/ops.rs:117-134) needs a `parent` arg, or agents can only ever post at top level.\n\n## Rendering\nIndentation in the comment list (:710-738) is the easy part. Decide the depth policy up front — unbounded nesting on a resizable sidebar-width pane degrades fast. Two levels (comment + replies, no deeper) is what most trackers settle on and is much cheaper to render and to focus-manage.\n\n## Depends on / related\n- **PM-86** (`version` written but never read) — this is precisely the field that an older `pm` binary would silently drop on its next save, taking every reply's parent link with it and flattening the thread irreversibly. Strongly prefer landing PM-86's guard first; if that's not wanted, at least know the exposure.\n- **PM-84** — per-reply composers multiply focusable inputs.\n- **PM-2** (line-anchored comments from the diff gutter) — `Comment.anchor` (pm.rs:132) already exists and is unblocked now that PM-72 shipped. A threaded reply to an anchored comment should presumably inherit or ignore the anchor; worth settling once rather than twice.\n\n## Open question\nIs this actually wanted for **comments**, or for **replies to review comments** (the PM-2 diff-gutter flow)? Threading matters much more in a code-review context than on a ticket. If PM-2 is the real motivation, this should probably follow it rather than lead.\n\n## Verify\nPost a reply, confirm it persists to .pm/pm.json5 with the right `parent`, renders indented, survives a round-trip through both the GUI and `mcp__pm__get_ticket`, and that an existing flat ticket (every comment in this project today) still renders unchanged."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 70,
      "title": "fremantle: scaffold crate + move scroll.rs, decorations.rs",
      "body": "Part of PM-55 (phase 1/5).\n\nAdd `crates/fremantle` as a new workspace member (`gpui = { workspace = true }`, same git pin as pm-ui: `zed-industries/zed` branch `main`). Move `scroll.rs` (pure math: `ScrollState`, `Axis`, `ScrollDrag`, thumb sizing — zero domain coupling) and `decorations.rs` (window chrome: rounded corners/shadow/resize grips) into it near-verbatim. pm-ui takes a path dep on fremantle, same convention as its existing dep on pm-core.\n\nLowest-risk phase — mainly proves out the workspace wiring before the harder migrations (theme, text-input, list primitive).\n\nVerify: `cargo check`/`cargo build` across the workspace; pm-ui still runs and scroll/window-decoration behavior is unchanged.",
      "status": "done",
      "priority": "normal",
      "labels": [
        "fremantle"
      ],
      "assignee": null,
      "author": "reaganiwadha",
      "created": 1788590656,
      "updated": 1788592841,
      "anchors": [],
      "comments": [],
      "history": [
        {
          "at": 1788592841,
          "author": "reaganiwadha",
          "kind": "status_changed",
          "old": "open",
          "new": "done"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 71,
      "title": "fremantle: Theme system (closes PM-18)",
      "body": "Part of PM-55 (phase 2/5). Closes PM-18.\n\npm-ui's `theme.rs` today is just flat `pub const` hex colors (`BG`, `PANEL`, `BORDER`, `TEXT`, `DIM`, `SELECT`, `ADD_BG`, `DEL_BG`, `CHANGED`, `CLOSE_HOVER`) plus pixel-metric constants and a rem-scaling helper — no struct, no light/dark support. Every one of pm-ui's 15+ view files does `use crate::theme::*` or imports individual constants directly.\n\nDesign a `Theme` struct/trait in fremantle holding the same tokens (colors + metrics + rem-scaling), instantiable so each consuming app supplies its own palette (paves the way for light/dark or per-app themes). Migrate pm-ui's `theme.rs` to a concrete `Theme` instance passed via gpui context (e.g. a global or `Entity<Theme>`), and update all call sites off `use crate::theme::*`.\n\nThis is the highest-touch migration (touches nearly every pm-ui view file) — do it as its own phase, after PM-55 phase 1 has proven the workspace wiring.\n\nVerify: `cargo check`/`cargo build`; visual smoke-test of pm-ui confirming colors/metrics are pixel-identical to before the migration.",
      "status": "done",
      "priority": "normal",
      "labels": [
        "fremantle"
      ],
      "assignee": null,
      "author": "reaganiwadha",
      "created": 1788590660,
      "updated": 1788595622,
      "anchors": [],
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "author": "reaganiwadha",
          "created": 1788595622,
          "body": "Implemented the full runtime migration (Zed's Global + ActiveTheme ext-trait pattern, not the lighter const-derivation option). `fremantle::theme::Theme { appearance, colors: ThemeColors, metrics: ThemeMetrics, base_rem }` installed once via `fremantle::theme::set_theme(cx, ...)` at the top of `Pm::new`, read anywhere via `cx.theme()`. pm-ui's `theme.rs` now just builds one concrete `Theme` value (`build()`) with every old literal preserved exactly, and re-exports `ActiveTheme` so existing `use crate::theme::*;` call sites picked up `.theme()` with no import changes needed.\n\nMigrated all ~260 call sites across 10 files (rgb(CONST) -> cx.theme().colors.x, px(CONST) -> px(cx.theme().metrics.x), rm()/scale_of() -> methods on Theme). A few free helper functions with no `cx` in scope (`chip`, `text_block` in tickets_view.rs, `image_divider`/`sidebar_resize_handle`, `round_bottom` in status_bar.rs) gained an explicit color/metric or `cx` parameter instead, resolved at their call sites. Full workspace test suite passes (33 tests); `cargo check --workspace` clean, no warnings.",
          "anchor": null
        }
      ],
      "history": [
        {
          "at": 1788595622,
          "author": "reaganiwadha",
          "kind": "commented",
          "comment_id": 1
        },
        {
          "at": 1788595622,
          "author": "reaganiwadha",
          "kind": "status_changed",
          "old": "open",
          "new": "done"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 72,
      "title": "fremantle: TextInput primitive + undo/redo (unblocks PM-2)",
      "body": "Part of PM-55 (phase 3/5). Unblocks PM-2.\n\nMove `text_input.rs` (971 lines) into fremantle as a `TextInput` primitive. It's already a full custom `Element` (IME support via `window.handle_input` + `EntityInputHandler`, single-line/multiline modes, actions-based editing: backspace, word/line motions, selection, copy/cut/paste, confirm/newline) and already domain-free, but its own doc comment states \"not handled: undo/redo\" — add that.\n\nPM-2 (\"wire line-anchored comments from the diff gutter\") is explicitly blocked on this: \"Blocked on a real text-input widget — the current one is a stopgap,\" anchored to `diff_view.rs:698-970`. Before closing this ticket, confirm/extend whatever API that usage actually needs (e.g. multi-field forms, submit-on-enter integration) so PM-2 can resume once this lands.\n\nVerify: `cargo check`/`cargo build`; exercise the text input in pm-ui (typing, IME, selection, undo/redo) via the `/run` skill.",
      "status": "done",
      "priority": "normal",
      "labels": [
        "fremantle"
      ],
      "assignee": null,
      "author": "reaganiwadha",
      "created": 1788590665,
      "updated": 1788622341,
      "anchors": [],
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "author": "claude",
          "created": 1788622341,
          "body": "Shipped in commit 3925d0c (\"fremantle: move TextInput into crate, add undo/redo\"). `crates/fremantle/src/text_input.rs` is now 1056 lines, with `UNDO_GROUP_INTERVAL` (300ms coalescing, :33), `UndoEntry` (:36), and Undo/Redo actions (:41-74). Closing.\n\nFollow-on work spun out rather than left here: PM-2 (its stated blocker was this widget) is now unblocked, and PM-82/83/84 cover the focus-handling half.",
          "anchor": null
        }
      ],
      "history": [
        {
          "at": 1788622328,
          "author": "claude",
          "kind": "status_changed",
          "old": "open",
          "new": "done"
        },
        {
          "at": 1788622341,
          "author": "claude",
          "kind": "commented",
          "comment_id": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 73,
      "title": "fremantle: generalize icons.rs (asset source from consumer)",
      "body": "Part of PM-55 (phase 4/5).\n\n`icons.rs` (330 lines) bundles SVGs via `include_dir!` pointed at pm-ui's own `assets/` dir, plus extension→icon-key tables. Move it into fremantle and parameterize the asset source (accept a byte-slice/`Dir` handle or an asset-provider trait from the consumer) instead of hardcoding pm-ui's asset path, so each app can supply its own SVG set.\n\nVerify: `cargo check`/`cargo build`; icons still render correctly in pm-ui after the asset source is passed in explicitly.",
      "status": "open",
      "priority": "normal",
      "labels": [
        "fremantle"
      ],
      "assignee": null,
      "author": "reaganiwadha",
      "created": 1788590668,
      "updated": 1788622778,
      "anchors": [],
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "author": "claude",
          "created": 1788622778,
          "body": "Phase status refresh: phases 1-3 of PM-55 have landed (PM-70 scaffold + scroll/decorations `552dd64`, PM-71 Theme `f005df5`, PM-72 TextInput `3925d0c`). This is next, with PM-74 last.\n\nTwo details from the current tree worth having before starting:\n- `include_dir!(\"$CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR/assets\")` is at pm-ui/src/icons.rs:10, and `bytes()` (:12) falls back to `file.svg` with `.expect(\"file.svg present\")` (:17) — i.e. it **panics** if the consumer's asset set lacks that one file. Whatever the asset-source abstraction ends up being, that implicit \"you must ship a file.svg\" contract needs to become explicit or fallible.\n- The extension tables (`FILE_STEMS_BY_ICON_KEY` :27, `FILE_SUFFIXES_BY_ICON_KEY`, `FILE_ICONS`, `lookup_key` :243) are a *file-type* mapping ported from Zed — arguably a separate concern from \"load an SVG by name\". A consumer might want fremantle's icon loading without a filename→icon-key table. Worth deciding whether both move or only the loader.\n\nAlso note `chevron_bytes` (:296) is used by tree_view.rs, so PM-74 depends on whatever shape this lands in. There are tests at :311-330 to carry across.",
          "anchor": null
        }
      ],
      "history": [
        {
          "at": 1788622778,
          "author": "claude",
          "kind": "commented",
          "comment_id": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 74,
      "title": "fremantle: generic list/row primitive (list_view, tree_view, history_view)",
      "body": "Part of PM-55 (phase 5/5, largest/riskiest — do last).\n\n`list_view.rs`, `tree_view.rs`, and `history_view.rs` share a generic virtualized-row/scrollbar rendering pattern, but all three are entangled with `Entity<Pm>` (pm's domain/app entity) rather than generic data.\n\nExtract the shared pattern into a delegate-based `fremantle::list` primitive — something like a `ListDelegate` trait providing row count + a row-render closure, similar to gpui's own list patterns — then rebuild pm-ui's three call sites as thin delegates supplying `Pm`-specific data.\n\nDo this only after phases 1-3 (workspace scaffolding, Theme, TextInput) have proven the extraction pattern, since this is the highest-risk migration.\n\nVerify: `cargo check`/`cargo build`; visual smoke-test of pm-ui's ticket list, file tree, and commit history views (scrolling, selection, row rendering) via the `/run` skill.",
      "status": "open",
      "priority": "normal",
      "labels": [
        "fremantle"
      ],
      "assignee": null,
      "author": "reaganiwadha",
      "created": 1788590671,
      "updated": 1788622789,
      "anchors": [],
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "author": "claude",
          "created": 1788622789,
          "body": "Phase status refresh: phases 1-3 of PM-55 have landed (PM-70 `552dd64`, PM-71 `f005df5`, PM-72 `3925d0c`), so the extraction pattern this ticket was waiting to see proven is now proven. PM-73 (icons) is the remaining prerequisite — `tree_view.rs` uses `chevron_bytes` and `icon_bytes_for`, so its asset-source shape needs to settle first.\n\nConcrete inventory for whoever picks this up. The three views are the same custom `Element` skeleton with different row content:\n\n| | file | struct | prepaint | element impl |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Changes | list_view.rs (466) | `ListView{pm}` :21 | `ListPrepaint` :44-60 | :62-320, `register_mouse` :325 |\n| Explorer | tree_view.rs (440) | `TreeView{pm}` :18 | `TreePrepaint` :42 | :61-320 |\n| History | history_view.rs (437) | `HistoryView{pm}` :18 | `HistoryPrepaint` :41 | :76-320 |\n\nAll three already import `fremantle::scroll::{Axis, BarInfo, ScrollDrag}` (e.g. list_view.rs:14), so the scroll math is **already shared** — what's triplicated is row virtualization (shape only `first..last`), scrollbar painting, hover/selection quads, and mouse registration. That's the actual extraction target.\n\nThe entanglement is that each holds `pm: Entity<Pm>` and reads `Pm` fields directly during prepaint, which is what the `ListDelegate` trait has to displace.\n\nTwo things to fix while extracting rather than carrying across:\n- `ADD_FG`/`DEL_FG` are hardcoded at list_view.rs:18-19, outside the theme — see PM-18 and PM-87, which are both chasing the same class of leak.\n- `rel_time()` lives in history_view.rs:59 but is used by tickets_view.rs too. It's a general utility sitting in a view file; it should land somewhere sensible in this move.\n\nThe ticket list itself (tickets_view.rs:365-427) is deliberately **not** one of these — it's plain `div`s in an `overflow_y_scroll` container, not a virtualized element. If PM-62 (kanban) or a longer backlog makes that a problem, it becomes a fourth consumer of whatever lands here.",
          "anchor": null
        }
      ],
      "history": [
        {
          "at": 1788622789,
          "author": "claude",
          "kind": "commented",
          "comment_id": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 75,
      "title": "Tickets: search bar to filter the ticket list",
      "body": "Add a text search input to the tickets list view (not global/spotlight search — that's tracked separately in PM-20). Typing should filter the currently-listed tickets by title (and probably id/display_id, maybe body) as-you-type, combined with the existing status filter.\n\nContext: `crates/pm-ui/src/tickets_view.rs` already has a status-based filter — a `Filter (n/5) ▾` button (`filter_button`, tickets_view.rs:168) opening a checklist popover, applied via `.filter(|t| self.ticket_filter.contains(&t.status))` (tickets_view.rs:227). A text search should live alongside that in the list header and compose with it (AND, not replace).\n\nDepends on a real text-input widget to host the query — PM-2 notes the current text input is a stopgap; PM-55/PM-72 (fremantle's TextInput primitive) is the tracked fix for that, so this ticket may want to wait on PM-72 landing, or use the existing stopgap if that's acceptable short-term.\n\nOpen questions to settle before implementing:\n- Match scope: title only, or also id/body/labels?\n- Case-insensitive substring match seems like the obvious default — confirm.\n- Where the input sits in the header relative to the Filter button (PM-63 \"UI more obvious about what filters is being selected\" may want to unify both into one visible filter-state affordance).",
      "status": "done",
      "priority": "normal",
      "labels": [
        "tickets",
        "ui"
      ],
      "assignee": null,
      "author": "reaganiwadha",
      "created": 1788590846,
      "updated": 1788622344,
      "anchors": [],
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "author": "reaganiwadha",
          "created": 1788590999,
          "body": "Let's have it scoped to title body and label, but weight them nicely, case insensitive, add a search icon button that reveals a search box and pushes the list layout below, animated if possible. and grabs focus of the cursor to there. No need pressing enter it should be fast. Use a fuzzy search library.",
          "anchor": null
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "author": "claude",
          "created": 1788622344,
          "body": "Shipped in commit 80b6b1a (\"Tickets: search bar with narrow-to-select\"). `search_toggle_button` at tickets_view.rs:184-214, filtering folded into `shown_tickets` (:274-286) alongside the existing status filter, `autoselect_on_narrow` (:291-300) wired via `cx.subscribe` in app.rs:222-226. Ctrl+F to reach it landed separately as PM-80. Closing.",
          "anchor": null
        }
