    {
      "id": 87,
      "title": "fremantle: purge the remaining pm-isms from the primitives",
      "body": "PM-77 (commit 0c60141) scrubbed fremantle's **doc comments** of pm assumptions. The *structural* leaks survived, and they matter more — they're in type signatures and public names, so they're what a second consumer actually trips over. PM-78's gallery will be the first thing to hit them.\n\n## The leaks\n\n**1. The action namespace is still `pm_`.** `actions!(pm_text_input, [...])` — crates/fremantle/src/text_input.rs:41, 27 actions. A crate whose whole premise is \"not shaped to any one app\" publishes its keyboard actions under the app's name. Renaming changes the action names consumers bind against, so it also touches `bind_text_input_keys` (src/main.rs:145-178). Do this one first: it's mechanical, and it gets more expensive with every consumer.\n\n**2. `ScrollDrag.col: usize`** — scroll.rs:47, documented as \"Which text column the drag started in (0 left, 1 right). Ignored for `Axis::Y`\". That is the side-by-side diff's two-pane model baked into a general scroll primitive. Options: make it a generic `lane: usize` / `slot: u32` with no prescribed meaning, or drop it from `ScrollDrag` and let the consumer carry its own drag context alongside. scroll.rs is the one fremantle module with tests (:97-134), so this is low-risk to change.\n\n**3. `ThemeMetrics` is a pm layout sheet.** theme.rs:37-62, 23 fields — `diff_split_min`, `diff_split_max`, `gutter_w`, `gutter_pad`, `text_pad_l`, `sidebar_min`, `sidebar_max_margin`, `section_header_h`, `section_split_h`, `tree_row_h`, `tree_indent`, `list_row_h`, `title_bar_h`, `status_bar_h`. A non-diff app has no `diff_split_max`. The struct's own doc (theme.rs:20) admits it: \"Named colors for every surface pm-ui (or another consumer) paints.\"\n\nWanted shape: fremantle keeps only what its own primitives read, and consumers attach their app metrics as an extension. Worth checking what fremantle actually needs first — `client_decoration_rounding`/`shadow` (used by decorations.rs) and the font/row metrics read by text_input are probably the whole list. Note `decorations.rs` doesn't even use the theme consistently today: `BORDER_SIZE` (:39) and the shadow color (:100) are hardcoded rather than coming from the `DecorationStyle` it was given.\n\n**4. Colors that bypass the theme entirely** — not in fremantle, but the same disease from the other end. `Status::color()` (pm-core/src/pm.rs:49), `Priority::color()` (:94) and `ChangeStatus::color()` (git.rs:65) return raw `u32` hex from the **data layer**, and list_view.rs:18-19 hardcodes `ADD_FG`/`DEL_FG`. PM-18 needs these on `ThemeColors` before a light scheme can work; noting it here so the two tickets don't each half-do it. Recommend PM-18 owns this item and this ticket owns 1-3.\n\n## Sequencing\nIndependent of PM-73/PM-74 (the remaining PM-55 phases) and safe to do alongside them — but do it **before** PM-78's gallery, so the gallery is written against the cleaned-up names rather than becoming a second site to update.\n\n## Verify\n`cargo check`/`cargo build` across the workspace; smoke-test pm-ui via the `/run` skill with attention to the text-input keymap (the action rename is exactly the change that compiles fine and silently unbinds every key).",
      "status": "open",
      "priority": "normal",
      "labels": [
        "fremantle"
      ],
      "assignee": null,
      "author": "claude",
      "created": 1788622439,
      "updated": 1788622439,
      "anchors": [],
      "comments": [],
      "history": [
        {
          "at": 1788622439,
          "author": "claude",
          "kind": "labels_changed",
          "old": [],
          "new": [
            "fremantle"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 88,
      "title": "Build variants: `cargo run` opens a distinct debug preview (own binary name, icon, window identity) so it can run beside the real pm",
      "body": "## The problem\nThere is exactly one `pm` today, and debugging it means closing the one you actually use. Worse, a coding agent that launches pm to test a change is indistinguishable — same executable name, same icon, same window — from the pm you have open with your real tickets in it.\n\nWanted: two clearly-marked variants that coexist.\n- **`cargo run`** → a *release preview* build (the thing you keep open).\n- **`cargo run` for the debug variant** → a **debug preview**: obviously different at a glance, and separately addressable.\n\n## What exists today\n- One binary, `pm`, defined by the root `Cargo.toml` `[package]` (name = \"pm\", v0.0.5). Workspace members are the four `crates/*`; the root package is the only bin target.\n- **No `.cargo/config.toml` exists** — so there are no cargo aliases yet. That's the natural home for `cargo run` shorthands.\n- `[profile.dev]` already sets `opt-level = 2` for itself and all deps (root Cargo.toml), with the comment \"gpui does real per-frame layout/text work; unoptimized it feels laggy\". So the dev build is *already* semi-optimised — the release/debug distinction wanted here is about **identity and marking**, not optimisation level.\n- The window icon is embedded at build time on Windows by `build.rs` from `assets/icon.ico` via `winresource`, failing soft with a warning. The runtime (X11) icon comes from a separate `ICON` static consumed in `open_pm_window` (src/main.rs:201-215).\n- `WindowOptions` (src/main.rs:203-214) sets bounds, a transparent client-decorated titlebar, min size and icon. The window *title* is set separately and deferred out of render (app.rs:898-906) because of a re-entrancy abort.\n- `#![cfg_attr(not(debug_assertions), windows_subsystem = \"windows\")]` (src/main.rs:10) — release has no console, debug does. Already a real behavioural fork between the two.\n\n## Scope (per the decision on 2026-09-05)\nThe debug preview differs by: **icon colour**, **window title marking**, **a distinct window/app identity**, and **its own binary name** (e.g. `pm-debug.exe`).\n\nConfig and ticket store are **shared** — deliberately, so debugging exercises your real data. Flagged as an open question below, because it has teeth.\n\n## Implementation sketch — pick one of two shapes\n**(a) A cargo feature** (`--features debug-preview`) read via `cfg!` for the name/icon/title. Simple; but `[package] name` can't vary by feature, so the binary name has to come from `[[bin]]` targets or a build-script rename, and feature-unification bugs are easy to hit.\n\n**(b) A second `[[bin]]` target** in the root package (`pm` and `pm-debug`), both thin `main`s over the same `pm-ui`/`pm-core` libs, differing in a handful of constants. More explicit, gives a real distinct executable name for free, and makes `cargo run --bin pm-debug` the honest command. **Recommend (b)**, with `.cargo/config.toml` aliases so the day-to-day commands stay short.\n\nEither way the variant identity should be one value threaded through: executable name, `assets/icon-debug.ico` (+ the X11 runtime icon), the window title prefix (app.rs:404 builds the title lead), and the app/window id.\n\nNote `build.rs` currently hardcodes `assets/icon.ico`; it needs to select per target.\n\n## The MCP angle — this is the part that bites\nThe stated symptom is \"MCP is flaky when I `cargo run`\". I checked the actual wiring, and the obvious explanation does **not** hold:\n\n- The server is registered as `{\"command\": \"pm\", \"args\": [\"--mcp\"]}` (`~/.claude.json`, written by `pm --setup`, crates/pm-core/src/setup.rs:385-421).\n- `pm` on PATH resolves to the **installed release** binary at `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Programs\\pm\\pm.exe`.\n- `cargo run` writes `target\\debug\\pm.exe` — a different file. So a rebuild cannot be locking or overwriting the running MCP server's executable.\n\nThree mechanisms that *are* real, and that this ticket should fix or at least document:\n\n1. **`install.ps1:37` — `Get-Process pm -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Stop-Process -Force`.** This kills *every* process named `pm`, by name, with no path check. That includes the running MCP server **and** any debug build you have open. So `--update`, or re-running the installer, silently severs the agent's MCP connection. A distinct binary name fixes half of this by construction; the installer should also match on path, not name.\n2. **`pm --update`** (`run_self_update`, crates/pm-core/src/update.rs:88-126) renames the live `pm.exe` → `pm.exe.old` and swaps in a new one, while an MCP server may be running from it.\n3. **If the server is ever registered from source** — the README explicitly suggests `{\"command\": \"cargo\", \"args\": [\"run\", \"-q\", \"-p\", \"pm\", \"--\", \"--mcp\"]}` (crates/pm-mcp/README.md:55) — then the MCP server *holds cargo's build lock on `target/`*, and every concurrent `cargo run`/`cargo check` blocks on \"waiting for file lock on build directory\" until it exits. That is a genuine deadlock-shaped flakiness and it's in our own docs as a recommendation.\n\n**So the variant should extend to MCP**: a `pm-debug --mcp` that a second agent session can register independently, without either one's rebuild-and-restart cycle disturbing the other. Worth deciding whether the debug MCP server should be registered under a different server name (`pm-debug`) to make it obvious which one an agent is talking to.\n\nAlso relevant: `open_project` (pm-mcp/src/ops.rs:237-256) locates the GUI via `$PM_BIN` → a sibling `pm`/`pm.exe` → `pm` on PATH. With two binaries that resolution becomes ambiguous — the debug MCP server should launch the debug GUI.\n\n## Open questions\n1. **Shared config is riskier than it sounds.** `~/.pm/config.json` holds `ui_scale`, `author`, `recent`, `watchjump` and the per-project store registry, and `ConfigStore::update` (pm-ui/src/config.rs:113-137) rewrites the whole file. Two pm processes running at once already race on it; two *variants* makes that routine rather than rare. Is shared config genuinely wanted, or shared **ticket store** with a separate config? The store is the part you want shared for debugging; the config is the part that will corrupt.\n2. Should the debug variant also get a different **window class / app id** on Linux, so the taskbar separates them (and not just a different title)? Same question for the Windows AppUserModelID.\n3. Should `cargo run` with no arguments open the release preview or the debug one? The framing above says release preview is yours and the agent uses debug — but the agent will run bare `cargo run` unless told otherwise, so the alias names need to make the wrong one hard to type by accident.\n4. Does the release preview differ from a *shipped* release at all, or is \"release preview\" just `cargo run --release`?\n\n## Verify\nBoth variants open simultaneously, visibly distinct by icon and title, each addressable as its own window. `cargo run` in each mode produces the expected executable name. Register `pm-debug --mcp` alongside `pm --mcp` and confirm rebuilding one does not disturb the other's MCP session. Then re-run the installer with a debug build open and confirm it no longer kills it (issue 1 above).",
      "status": "done",
      "priority": "high",
      "labels": [],
      "assignee": null,
      "author": "claude",
      "created": 1788623489,
      "updated": 1788627916,
      "anchors": [],
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "author": "claude",
          "created": 1788626533,
          "body": "Shipped the GUI variant + MCP entry point (shape (b), per the decisions).\n\n**Structure:** root package split into a `pm` lib + two thin `[[bin]]` targets. `src/lib.rs` holds `run(variant: Variant)` and all the wiring that was in `main.rs`; `src/main.rs` → `pm::run(pm::RELEASE)`, new `src/bin/pm-debug.rs` → `pm::run(pm::DEBUG)`. `default-run = \"pm\"` keeps bare `cargo run` = release preview; `.cargo/config.toml` adds `cargo pmd`.\n\n**Variant identity threaded through:**\n- `cx.set_app_identity(app_id, label)` — Windows AUMID.\n- `WindowOptions.app_id` — Linux `_NET_WM_CLASS` (was never set before).\n- Window title: `pm-ui` gets a process-global `set_app_label` / `app_label()` (OnceLock, defaults `\"pm\"`), consumed by `window_title()` (app.rs) — feeds both the OS title and the in-window title bar.\n- Icon: runtime amber tint of the loaded `icon.png` for the debug build (`tint_debug` in lib.rs) — no new asset.\n- `--version` / `--help`: `buildinfo::long_version_named(prog)` and `cli::usage(prog)`; `pm-debug --version` → `pm-debug 0.0.5 (…)`.\n- `pm-mcp` `locate_gui` now prefers a sibling matching the server's own exe stem, so `pm-debug --mcp` launches the `pm-debug` GUI.\n\n**Verified:** `cargo build` produces `pm.exe` + `pm-debug.exe`; `pm-debug .` opens alongside running `pm.exe` processes without conflict; `--version`/`--help` text correct; `cargo test` (all green) and clippy (only pre-existing warnings) clean.\n\n**Deferred → PM-96:** `pm-debug --setup` / registry keys / Start Menu / uninstaller / self-update / installer are all still `pm`-hardcoded in `pm_core::setup` + `update.rs` + `install.ps1`. PM-88 issue 1 (`Get-Process pm | Stop-Process`) is moot for a distinct `pm-debug.exe`. Issues 2–3 (self-update swap, `cargo run --mcp` build lock) don't affect a `cargo run` debug build; the README build-lock note folds into PM-90. Embedded `.exe`-file icon stays shared (winresource is one-resource-per-crate) — runtime icon + AUMID cover the visible cases.",
          "anchor": null
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "author": "claude",
          "created": 1788627653,
          "body": "Follow-up (7c8a2d8): replaced the runtime `tint_debug` recolour with a real asset — `assets/icon-debug.png`, generated by hue-shifting `icon.png` +185° (orange → blue) with Pillow. `Variant` now carries `icon_png: &'static [u8]`; `DEBUG` does `include_bytes!(\"../assets/icon-debug.png\")`. Embedded `.exe`-file icon still shared (winresource limitation, noted above).",
          "anchor": null
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "author": "claude",
          "created": 1788627916,
          "body": "Correction: on Windows, gpui **ignores `WindowOptions.icon`** — its Windows backend calls `LoadImageW(module, PCWSTR(1), IMAGE_ICON, …)`, i.e. the embedded `.exe` resource id 1 (from build.rs), for both the window class and taskbar. The RgbaImage is X11-only. So `pm-debug` showed `pm`'s orange icon on Windows regardless of the runtime png.\n\nReal fix (this commit): `pm-debug` is now its own package `crates/pm-debug` with its own `build.rs` embedding `assets/icon-debug.ico` (winresource is one resource per crate — that's exactly why the split is needed). The root package keeps `[lib] pm` + `[[bin]] pm`; `src/bin/pm-debug.rs` deleted; `cargo pmd` → `run -p pm-debug`. Verified the two `.exe`s carry different embedded icon blobs. The earlier \"known gap: shared embedded icon\" is now closed.",
          "anchor": null
        }
      ],
      "history": [
        {
          "at": 1788623489,
          "author": "claude",
          "kind": "priority_changed",
