    {
      "id": 91,
      "title": "MCP: a search/query tool over tickets (mirror what PM-75 shipped in the GUI)",
      "body": "## The gap\n`list_tickets` (crates/pm-mcp/src/lib.rs:126-130, args at :44-52) filters on exactly two things: `status` and `label`. There is no text search of any kind.\n\nThe GUI is ahead here — **PM-75** shipped fuzzy search over title, body and labels with narrow-to-select (tickets_view.rs:184-214, filtering in `shown_tickets` :274-286). MCP got none of it.\n\nSo an agent asking the most common question there is — *\"is there already a ticket about this?\"* — has to list all 89 tickets and read the titles. That's how duplicates get filed, and it's a poor use of context for what should be one call returning three candidates.\n\n## In scope\nA query capability over the ticket store. Either a new `search_tickets` tool or a `query` argument on `list_tickets` — the latter is probably better, since it composes with the existing `status`/`label` filters rather than creating a second entry point that has to re-implement them.\n\nMatch scope should follow what PM-75 settled on for the GUI: **title, body and labels, weighted, case-insensitive**. Keeping the two surfaces consistent matters more than either being individually optimal — an agent and a human searching the same words should find the same tickets.\n\nThe GUI uses a fuzzy library. Worth deciding whether MCP shares that implementation (put the matcher in `pm-core` so both call it) or does something simpler. Sharing is the obvious call and would let PM-75's weighting be tuned once.\n\n## Also want\n- Return **ranked** results with scores, not an unordered filtered list — the point is \"the three most likely matches\", not \"everything containing this substring\".\n- Include enough per hit to decide without a follow-up `get_ticket`: at minimum a body excerpt around the match. This overlaps the bulk-read ticket; settle the response shape across both.\n- Search **comments** too, or not? Comments carry a lot of the real reasoning in this project (PM-44's scoping notes, PM-79's split recommendation). Leaning yes, flagged as an open question because it changes the result shape — a hit on a comment isn't a hit on a ticket.\n\n## Related\n- **PM-75** — the GUI equivalent, already shipped; share the matcher.\n- The `create_ticket` dedupe ticket depends on this — dedupe is just this search run automatically at file time.\n- **PM-20** (spotlight-style global search) is the other search surface; if a shared matcher lands in `pm-core` it serves all three.\n\n## Verify\nSearch for terms that appear only in a body (e.g. \"ConPTY\", which is in PM-60's comment) and only in a title, and confirm both are found and sensibly ranked. Compare results against the GUI search for the same query — they should agree.",
      "status": "open",
      "priority": "high",
      "labels": [
        "mcp"
      ],
      "assignee": null,
      "author": "claude",
      "created": 1788624567,
      "updated": 1788624567,
      "anchors": [],
