            "tickets"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 96,
      "title": "pm-debug: namespace --setup / registry / installer / self-update",
      "body": "Follow-up carved out of PM-88, which shipped the `pm-debug` GUI variant + MCP entry point but deliberately deferred the Windows install/registration surface.\n\n## Still hardcoded to `pm`\n- `crates/pm-core/src/setup.rs` — `UNINSTALL_KEY` / `APP_PATHS_KEY` consts (`...\\Uninstall\\pm`, `...\\App Paths\\pm.exe`), the Start Menu `pm.lnk` (`create_start_menu_shortcut`), the uninstaller `DisplayName` `\"pm (Plus Minus)\"`, and the MCP server name (`claude mcp add pm ...` + the `mcpServers.pm` key + `command: \"pm\"` in `claude_json_edit`). Running `pm-debug --setup` today would collide with `pm`'s entries.\n- `crates/pm-core/src/update.rs` — `latest()` hardcodes the `pm.exe` release-asset name and the \"pm is up to date\" text. `run_self_update` keys off `current_exe()` so the swap itself is name-agnostic, but a `pm-debug` self-update makes no sense (debug builds are `cargo run`); probably `pm-debug --update` should just refuse.\n- `install.ps1` — installs only `pm`. PM-88 issue 1 (`Get-Process pm | Stop-Process`) is already moot for a distinct `pm-debug.exe` (exact-match), but if the installer ever ships `pm-debug` it needs path-scoped matching.\n\n## Suggested approach\nThread the `Variant` (or just its label + a reverse-DNS id) from `pm`/`pm-mcp` into `pm_core::setup` so every key/name/shortcut is namespaced. Register the debug MCP server under the name `pm-debug` in `~/.claude.json` so an agent can tell which one it's talking to. Decide whether `pm-debug --setup` is even wanted vs. \"wire it by hand with `claude mcp add pm-debug -- <path> --mcp`\".\n\n## Open question\nDoes `pm-debug` need Start Menu / uninstaller entries at all, or only the MCP registration? A `cargo run` build arguably needs neither.",
      "status": "open",
      "priority": "normal",
      "labels": [
        "mcp"
      ],
      "assignee": null,
      "author": "claude",
      "created": 1788626518,
      "updated": 1788626518,
      "anchors": [],
      "comments": [],
      "history": [
