    },
    {
      "id": 97,
      "title": "pm.json5: round-trip unknown keys via a serde(flatten) catch-all",
      "body": "Split from PM-86, which stopped the bleeding (a too-new store is now read-only rather than silently truncated — `SCHEMA_VERSION` + `save_in` guard).\n\nThis is the stronger fix: add `#[serde(flatten)] extra: Map<String, Value>` catch-alls to `Ticket` and `Comment` (and maybe `PmData`/`Project`) in `crates/pm-core/src/pm.rs` so an older binary carries unknown fields through a save untouched instead of dropping them. With this in place, additive schema changes stop being breaking, and the `version` guard only needs to move for genuinely incompatible reshapes (PM-86's open question).\n\nDo this **before** the first schema addition lands (PM-69 `Comment.parent`, PM-50 ticket links, PM-33 attachments) — it only protects fields written after it exists.\n\nVerify: extend the pm.rs round-trip tests — a document with unknown keys on a ticket and a comment survives load→save byte-for-byte on those keys.",
      "status": "open",
      "priority": "normal",
      "labels": [],
      "assignee": null,
      "author": "claude",
      "created": 1788626929,
      "updated": 1788626929,
      "anchors": [],
      "comments": [],
      "history": []
    }
